{"id":"Plant-Doctor-ikw","content_hash":"8d441b2b274b99ecbeadff79ac0995d074b8f3f9eaf8ccf12f0cccf324265076","title":"Integrate DSPy/GEPA for prompt optimization to improve Haiku accuracy","description":"Successfully integrated GEPA for prompt optimization. Pilot results:\n- Original Haiku accuracy: 60%\n- Optimized accuracy: 80%\n- Improvement: +20%\n- Cost: $0.14 (100 metric calls)\n\nGEPA evolved the system prompt through 13 iterations, learning to:\n1. Include plant species in disease names\n2. Add domain-specific knowledge about common diseases\n3. Structure confidence scoring methodology\n4. Emphasize specificity over generalization\n\nFiles created:\n- backend/evals/dspy_optimizer.py - GEPA adapter and optimization logic\n- backend/evals/results/gepa_optimization.json - Optimization results\n\nNext steps:\n- Run larger optimization with more training data\n- Test optimized prompt on full 236-image dataset\n- Consider integrating optimized prompt into main.py","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-12-07T12:59:02.230209-08:00","updated_at":"2025-12-20T11:44:29.319629-08:00","closed_at":"2025-12-20T11:44:29.319629-08:00","source_repo":"."}
